        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r698219072-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "REAL culture",
        "text": "I had a guide and was grateful, without him I wouldn’t have gone in! We went on the last Monday of the nepal month so it was packed with women ending fasting. So much color and beauty! \n\nIt’s a real holy place. This is where end of life ceremonies and cremation take place along the river (so you may feel a bit uncomfortable) and people are there mourning. \n\nThe main temple is only for practicing Hindus and others are not let in. You will also be requested to remove shoes (unless it’s a madhouse like I saw!) \n\nThere are also little shops on the perimeter. The “temple” is actually many buildings, temples, river, park and more. ",
